<title>UK: Royal Bank sells Royal Scottish unit stake.</title>
<headline>Royal Bank sells Royal Scottish unit stake.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Bank of Scotland said on Tuesday it completed the sale of 30 percent of Royal Scottish Assurance Plc to Scottish Widows' Fund and Life Assurance Society.  </p>
<p>The Royal Bank of Scotland said the transaction included 14.7 million ordinary shares of one stg each.</p>
<p>The company did not disclose the price at which the stake was sold but said there was no material gain or loss on it.</p>
<p>&quot;The impact of the transaction on future earnings and net assets of Royal Bank of Scotland will not be material,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
